A sale price remains unknown when several SEK postings could represent settlement.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight transactions --id 8 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity SEK
  default
  format 1,000.00 SEK
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:CashA
account Assets:CashB
account Income:Other

2024-01-01 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 SEK}
  Assets:CashA  -100 SEK

2024-01-02 Sale with ambiguous settlement
  Assets:Fund  -1 FUND {100 SEK}
  Assets:CashA  120 SEK
  Assets:CashB  130 SEK
  Income:Other  -150 SEK

========== OUTPUT ==========

2024-01-02 Sale with ambiguous settlement
    Assets:Fund                         -1 FUND {100.00 SEK}
    Assets:CashA                          120.00 SEK
    Assets:CashB                          130.00 SEK
    Income:Other                         -150.00 SEK

========== WARNINGS ==========

[INVALID_COMMODITY_TRADE] Negative FUND posting must use both a lot cost ({...} or {{...}}) and a transaction price (@ or @@); the default commodity is SEK
  {{JOURNAL_PATH}}:16:3
